Subject: [PATCH] mtk: cpuidle: handle WFI-only remedy history without division

A full history buffer need not contain a non-WFI state. For example,
latency QoS can keep a CPU in WFI while its measured idle duration is
longer than the hidden-state threshold. Then nsamp is full and cnt is
zero, but total_cnt is also zero. The remedy-off branch divides by zero.

When there are no deep-state samples, return no remedy prediction. The
existing timer and latency-QoS state selection still applies. Preserve
the ratios, thresholds and decisions for all histories with samples.

This targets the Rodin vendor MHSP module, not the common boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
@@ -403,6 +403,9 @@
 			gov->predict_info |= PREDICT_ERR_REMEDY_THRES;
 		}
 	} else {
+		if (!gov->remedy.total_cnt)
+			return 0;
+
 		threshold = div_u64((gov->remedy.match_cnt * 100),
 				    gov->remedy.total_cnt);
 		gov->predict_info |= PREDICT_ERR_REMEDY_OFF_TIMES;
